{{also|Appendix:Variations of "but"}}
==Translingual==

===Etymology===
{{clip|mul|en:'''Bu'''ngain}} with {{m|mul|t}} as a placeholder.

===Symbol===
{{mul-symbol}}

# {{ISO 639|3}}

===See also===
* {{langcat}}

==English==
{{wp|BUT}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|but}}, {{m|enm|buten}}, {{m|enm|boute}}, {{m|enm|bouten}}, from {{inh|en|ang|būtan|t=without, outside of, except, only}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*biūtan}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*biūtini}}, equivalent to {{af|en|be-|out|nocat=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|but}}, {{m|sco|bot|t=outside, without, but}}, {{cog|stq|buute|t=without}}, {{cog|fy|bûten|t=outside of, apart from, other than, except, but}}, {{cog|nl|buiten|t=outside}}, {{cog|nds-nl|buten|t=outside}}, {{cog|nds-de|buuten}}, {{m|nds-de|buute|t=outside}}, obsolete {{cog|de|baußen|t=outside}}, {{cog|lb|baussen}}. Compare {{l|en|bin}}, {{l|en|about}}.

===Pronunciation===
