===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:capital<ety:bor<fro:capital<ety:bor<la:capitālis>>>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|capital}}, borrowed partly from {{der|en|fro|capital}} and partly from {{der|en|la|capitālis|t=of the head}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=capitā̆l|pos=adj|id=MED6727}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''adj.'' and ''n.''<sup>2</sup>|noformat=1|id=8654406974}}</ref> (in sense “head of [[cattle]]”), from {{m|la|caput|t=head}} ({{cog|en|cap}}) + {{m|la|-ālis|pos=suffix forming adjectives}}. Use in trade and finance originated in Medieval economies when a common but expensive transaction involved trading heads of cattle. The noun is from the adjective.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=capitā̆l|pos=''n.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED6725}}</ref> In the fourth sense, displaced native {{noncog|ang|hēafodburg}}, equivalent to {{l|en|head}} + {{l|en|borough|t=city}}.

Compare {{m|en|chattel}} and {{m|en|kith and kine|t=all one’s possessions}}, which also use “cow” to mean “property”.

{{doublet|en|cattle|chattel}}.

