#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=I liked the man for his own sake, and even had he promised to turn out a celebrity it would have had no weight with me. I look upon notoriety with the same indifference as on the '''buttons''' on a man's shirt-front, or the crest on his note-paper.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author={{w|Xavier Herbert}}|title=Soldiers' Women|year_published=1978|publisher=Fontana Books|location=Netley, SA|page=88|passage=Rather should it be said that these ladies wore dress of military style, since there was nothing uniform about their outfits, one being in powder-blue with silver '''buttons''' and a forage-cap, the other in tan with gold '''buttons''' and the dinkiest of red-peaked kepis.}}
#: {{ux|en|April fastened the '''buttons''' of her overcoat to keep out the wind.}}
