# {{senseid|en|Q11946202}}A flying [[insect]] of the [[order]] {{taxfmt|Lepidoptera|order}}, distinguished from moths by their [[diurnal]] activity and generally brighter colouring. {{defdate|from 11th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Phoenix|title=[Autobiographical Fragment]|page=836|passage=It is true. I am like a '''butterfly''', and I shall only live a little while.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-11-24|author=Patrick Barkham| title=Pesticide may be reason butterfly numbers are falling in UK, says study| journal=w:The Guardian| url=http://www.theguardian.com/environment/2015/nov/24/pesticide-butterflies-declining-uk-study| passage=Dr Andre Gilburn, of the University of Stirling, who led the '''butterfly''' study, said: “Our study not only identifies a worrying link between the use of neonicotinoids and declines in '''butterflies''' but also suggests that the strength of their impact on many species could be huge.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305141932/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2015/nov/24/pesticide-butterflies-declining-uk-study}}
## {{lb|en|loosely}} The [[imago]] (final form) of such an insect, consisting usually of a long body with large flat wings, as opposed to earlier [[instar]]s such as [[caterpillar]] or [[pupa]].
##* {{quote-book|en|title=w:The Very Hungry Caterpillar|author=w:Eric Carle|year=1969|text=Then he nibbled a hole in the cocoon, pushed his way out and he was a beautiful '''butterfly'''!}}
# {{lb|en|medicine|attributive}} A use of surgical tape, cut into thin strips and placed across an open wound to hold it closed.
#: {{co|en|'''butterfly''' tape; '''butterfly''' bandage; '''butterfly''' strips}}
# {{senseid|en|Q245249}}{{lb|en|swimming}} The [[butterfly stroke]]. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
# Any of several plane curves that look like a butterfly; see {{w|Butterfly curve (transcendental)}} and {{w|Butterfly curve (algebraic)}}. {{C|en|Curves}}
# {{lb|en|in plural}} {{ellipsis of|en|butterflies in one's stomach|butterflies in one’s stomach|A sensation of excited anxiety felt in the stomach}}.
#: {{ux|en|I get terrible '''butterflies''' before an exam.}}
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} Someone seen as being [[unserious]] and (originally) [[dress#Verb|dressed ]] [[gaudily]]; someone [[flighty]] and [[unreliable]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Meredith Richard Feverel||15||He was affable; therefore he was frivolous. The women liked him; therefore he was a '''butterfly'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=Henry James|title=What Maisie Knew|passage=The day came indeed when her breathless auditors learnt from her in bewilderment that what ailed him was that he was, alas, simply not serious. Maisie wept on Mrs. Wix's bosom after hearing that Sir Claude was a '''butterfly'''{{nb...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} A combination of four [[option]]s of the same type at three [[strike price]]s giving limited profit and limited risk.
# {{lb|en|[[alternate history]]}} A [[random]] [[change]] in an [[aspect]] of the [[timeline]] seemingly unrelated to the primary [[point of divergence]], resulting from the [[butterfly effect]].
#: {{ux|en|One potential '''butterfly''' could be JFK having another son the year after the POD instead of a daughter.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A type of [[stretch]] in which one sits on the ground with the legs folded into a shape like that of a butterfly's wings, slightly rocking them up and down, resembling the wings [[flutter]]ing.
# A person who changes [[partners]] [[frequently]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.pattayaunlimited.com/paying-for-bar-girls-in-pattaya/|title=Paying For Bar Girls, Sex in Pattaya|date=December 9 2022|work=Pattaya Unlimited|author=Darren C|text=What does it mean to be a '''butterfly''' in Pattaya? It means, just like a '''butterfly''' briefly visits many flowers, you will briefly visit many different girls.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A safety link or detaching hook above the [[cage]] attached to the winding rope to prevent the cage from being overwound.
# {{lb|en|Philippines|Philippine politics|often|pejorative}} [[party]] [[switcher]]; [[turncoat]].
#: {{syn|en|balimbing|Thesaurus:defector}}

