===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|catirpel}}, {{m|enm|catirpeller}}, probably from {{der|en|fro-nor|catepeluse}} (Modern French {{m|fr|chatte}} + {{m|fr|pileuse||hairy cat}}), from {{der|en|la-lat|catta}} + {{m|la|pilōsa}}. The sense "rapacious, extortionate person" arose by association with obsolete {{m|en|piller||plunderer}}. See Modern Norman {{m|nrf|cattepeleuse}}. Displaced native {{m|en|kaleworm}}, from {{ncog|enm|cowle worm}}, {{m|enm|cale worme|t=caterpillar, corn weevil}}, from {{ncog|ang|cawelwyrm}}, {{m|ang|cawelwurm|t=caterpillar}}.

