===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|ḱóm}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*wreh₂ǵʰ-}}
[[File:Garganta del Diablo or Devil Throat Iguazu Falls Argentina Luca Galuzzi 2005.JPG|thumb|The [[w:Devil's Throat, Iguazu Falls|Devil’s Throat]], the largest cataract ''({{senseno|en|waterfall}})'' of the {{w|Iguazu Falls}} at the [[border#Noun|border]] of [[Argentina]] and [[Brazil]].]]

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{m|en|cataracts|t=|pos=noun (plural only)}}, from Late {{inh|en|enm|cataract}}, {{m|enm|cataracta}}, {{m|enm|cateract}}, {{m|enm|cateracte|t=floodgate of heaven}},<ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=cataracte|pos=n|id=MED6934}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|cataracte}} (modern {{cog|fr|cataracte}}), and from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|cataracta|t=floodgate; waterfall}}, from {{der|en|grc|καταρράκτης|καταρ(ρ)άκτης|(''noun'') waterfall; (''adjective'') rushing downwards}}, from {{m|grc|καταρρᾱ́σσω|καταρ(ρ)ᾱ́σσω|t=to pour down; to rush downwards}} + {{m|grc|-της|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming nouns denoting a state of being}}. {{m|grc||Καταρ(ρ)ᾱ́σσω}} is derived either:<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=3162968239|date=March 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

* from {{m|grc|κᾰτᾰ-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘downwards’}} + {{m|grc|ἀρᾰ́σσω|t=to dash to pieces; to strike}} (further etymology unknown, possibly {{glossary|onomatopoeic}}) or {{m|grc|ῥᾱ́σσω|t=to dash; to strike}} (possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wreh₂ǵʰ-|t=to pound, strike}}); or
* from {{m|grc|καταρρηγνύναι|t=to break down}}.

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1167701444|date=July 2023}}</ref>

