#* {{RQ:Drayton Poly-Olbion|chapter=The Sixt Song|page=88|passage=[T]he Salmon ſeekes a freſher ſtreame to find / {{...}} and ſtems the vvatry tract / VVhere ''Tivy'' falling dovvne, doth make a '''Cataract''', / Forc't by the riſing Rocks that there her courſe oppoſe, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Defoe New Voyage|part=II|page=190|passage=[C]oming dovvn farther the ſame River, they heard a terrible Noiſe in the River, as of a mighty '''Cataract''', or VVater-fall, vvhich increaſed as they came forvvard, till it grevv ſo loud, that they could not hear themſelves ſpeak, much leſs hear one another.}}
