#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|volume=II|poem=The Day-Dream|section=The Revival|page=156|passage=The palace bang'd, and buzz'd and clackt, / And all the long-pent stream of life / Dash'd downward in a '''cataract'''.}}
