===Etymology 2===
[[File:O. degus eye (cataract).jpg|thumb|A cataract ''({{senseno|en|ophthalmology}})'' in the [[eye#Noun|eye]] of a [[degu|common degu]] ({{taxlink|Octodon degus|species}}), a [[species]] of small [[rodent#Noun|rodent]].]]

{{root|en|ine-pro|*kleh₂w-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|cataract}}, {{m|enm|cataracta}}, {{m|enm|cateract}}, {{m|enm|cateracte|t=(''medicine'') clouding of the lens in the eye}},<ref name="MED"/> from {{der|en|fro|cataracte|t=clouding of the lens in the eye}}, and then either:<ref name="OED"/>

* from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|cataracta|t=portcullis}} (in the sense of something blocking vision as a portcullis blocks a gateway), from {{der|en|grc|καταρράκτης|καταρ(ρ)άκτης|act of rushing down; portcullis}} (see further at [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]]); or
* from {{m|la|clāthrāta}} (in {{m|la|[[fenestra]] [[clāthrāta]]|t=window grating}}), an {{glossary|inflected}} form of {{m|la|clāthrātus|t=grated, latticed, clathrate}}, from {{m|la|clāthrī|t=grate, lattic}} + {{m|la|-ātus|pos={{glossary|suffix}} denoting possession of something, forming {{glossary|adjective}}s from {{glossary|noun}}s}}. {{m|la||Clāthrī}} is derived from {{der|en|grc-dor|κλᾳ̃θρα}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kleh₂w-|*(s)kleh₂w-|crook, hook; peg; to close something}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|rare}} {{synonym of|en|portcullis|t=a [[gate#Noun|gate]] in the [[form#Noun|form]] of a [[grating#Noun|grating]] which is [[lower#Verb|lowered]] into [[place#Noun|place]] at the [[gateway#Noun|gateway]] of a [[castle#Noun|castle]], a [[fort#Noun|fort]], etc.}}; also, a [[window#Noun|window]] grating.
#* {{RQ:Rabelais Gargantua|volume=I|book=3|chapter=The Author's Prologue to the Third Book|page=315|passage=Others did fortifie and rampire their Walls, {{...}} assured the Port-culleys, fasten'd the Herses, Sarasinesks and '''Cataracks''', placed their Centries, and doubled their Patrouilee.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}}
## {{senseid|en|ophthalmology}}{{lb|en|ophthalmology|pathology}} A [[clouding#Noun|clouding]] of the [[lens#Noun|lens]] in the [[eye#Noun|eye]] [[lead#Verb|leading]] to a [[decrease#Noun|decrease]] in [[vision]].
##* {{RQ:Turberville Faulconrie|chapter=Of the Cataract in the Eyes of a Hawke|page=235|passage=[T]her is a '''Caratact''' which doth light vpon the eyes of a Hawke, whome we may tearme a ſuffuſion, a miſchiefe not ſafely remoued, and diuers times impoſſible to be recured, as namely whẽ {{quote-gloss|when}} it is growen too thicke, and ouerlong hath bin ſuffered in the eye, without ſeeking remedie for it: {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Cynthia Mattox; Helen K. Wu; Joel S. Schuman|chapter=Ocular Disorders of Aging|editors=Joseph J. Gallo; Jan Busby-Whitehead; Peter V. Rabins; Rebecca A. Silliman; John B. Murphy; William Reichel|title=Reichel’s Care of the Elderly: Clinical Aspects of Aging|edition=5th|location=Philadelphia, Pa.&#59; Baltimore, Md.|publisher=w:Lippincott Williams & Wilkins|section=section I (Care of the Elderly Patient: Evaluation, Diagnosis, and Management)|page=563|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/reichelscareofel00gall/page/563/mode/1up|column=2|isbn=978-0-683-30169-4|passage=Rarely, a dense, swollen neglected '''cataract''' precipitates an angle-closure glaucoma.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|date=22 June 2022|artist=w:Spiritbox|title=Rotoscope|album=Rotoscope|series=Rise 510-1|location=Beaverton, Or.|publisher=w:Rise Records|passage=Shallow, this is what I created / Splayed out skeletons in the cracks in the pavement / And now, can you feel the injection back behind those cloudy eyes? / In-between every '''cataract''', a projection of my life}}
### {{lb|en|figurative}} Something which [[obscure#Verb|obscures]].
###* {{quote-book|en|year=1631|author=w:Richard Brathwait|chapter=Decency|title=The English Gentlewoman, Drawne out to the Full Body:{{nb...|Expressing, what Habilliments doe Best Attire Her, what Ornaments doe best Adorne Her, what Complements doe best Accomplish Her.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed by}} B. Alsop and T. Fawcet, for Michaell Sparke,{{nb...|dwelling in Greene Arbor.}}|page=86|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/b30328925/page/86/mode/1up|oclc=1203227915|passage=Thoſe filmes vvhich darkened the ''eye'' of the mindes, are remoued, thoſe thicke '''Cataracts''' of earthly vanities are diſperſed and diſpelled, and a nevv light into a nevv heart infuſed.}}
## {{lb|en|obsolete|textiles}} A [[tool#Noun|tool]] [[use#Verb|used]] for [[break#Verb|breaking]] [[flax]]; a [[brake#Noun|brake]].
##* {{RQ:Rabelais Gargantua|volume=II|book=3|chapter=How the Famous Pantagruelion ought to be Prepared and Wrought|page=60|passage=Some modern Pantagruelists, to shun and avoid that manual Labour, which such a separating and partitional Work would of necessity require, employ certain Catarratick Instruments, {{...}} and athwart those '''Cataracts''' they break and bruise to very Trash the woody parcels {{quote-gloss|of the fictional herb “pantagruelion”}}, thereby to preserve the better the Fibres, which are the precious and excellent parts.}}

